arm64-darwin  cxx1 emits `__Unwind_Resume` and clang does not, on this target only - x86_64-linux and x86_64-windows agree name for name. It is a difference about which frames get a cleanup, not about mangling: cxx1 builds a landing pad for the guarded temporary in the skipped operand so an exception passing through destroys it, where clang proves the destructor unreachable for the elided temporary and emits no cleanup at all on Mach-O. The same case on ELF makes clang emit the pad too, which is why only this target differs. cxx1's pad is a superset - it runs the destructor the guard says exists and nothing otherwise - and the case links and runs identically on all three.
